.env*

# Container-built Rust artifacts (root-owned; see the containerized cargo loop).
# Also covers ad-hoc CARGO_TARGET_DIR scratch dirs (target-repro, target-localcheck…).
**/target-*/

# Local dev-only generated secrets (admin key, etc.) — never commit.
.dev-secrets
prod.secrets.env
# Throwaway owner keys the seed generates so the DEMO can sign agent mandates
# with the production code path. Disposable by construction, but they are still
# private keys and have no business in a public repository.
core/.demo-owner-keys.json
deploy/demo/

# Internal-only material. This repository is public: prospect lists, outreach
# plans, unreviewed legal templates and internal assessments stay local.
docs/EXTERNAL-REVIEW-*.md
docs/sales/icp-lead-brief.md
docs/sales/outreach-playbook.md
docs/sales/lead-list-*.xlsx
docs/legal/
# Internal pricing reasoning (it says so on line 3) and internal planning specs.
docs/sales/pricing-options.md
docs/superpowers/
.~lock.*#

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts


*/*/node_modules
*/node_modules

# WSL Windows zone metadata
*.Zone.Identifier
*:Zone.Identifier

# ── SauronID demo: private identity stays local; templates are committed ──────
# The real connection/identity file (GPU SSH target, VM host, admin key, core
# URL) and the Solana keypair are NEVER committed. The *.example templates are.
deploy/demo.local.env
deploy/secrets/
# No-Docker path: VM-side secret env files + locally-built artifacts stay out.
deploy/native/core.env
deploy/native/site.env
deploy/native/dist/
# Re-include the committed templates (negations must follow the broad .env.* rule).
!deploy/.env.deploy.example
!deploy/demo.local.env.example

# compiled example binaries
examples/go-quickstart/go-quickstart

# ── ZKP issuer-dependent e2e (untracked, kept on disk) ────────────────────────
# The ZKP issuer service went with the banking surface in 263fc0c and nothing
# replaced it: core/src/issuer_runtime.rs is a client, not a server. These
# scripts call zkp_require_issuer and hard-exit without one, so they cannot run
# and were holding the KYA E2E job red. Untracked rather than deleted — restore
# them from git history (or from disk) if a paying customer needs KYC/ZKP back.
core/tests/e2e_agent_matrix.sh
core/tests/e2e_ajwt_jti_replay.sh
core/tests/e2e_kya_autonomous.sh
core/tests/e2e_kya_delegated.sh
core/tests/e2e_ring_restore_consent.sh
core/tests/run_confidence_suite.sh
core/tests/hf_fetch_and_matrix_test.sh
core/tests/lib/zkp_fixture.sh
